- op: create  # 1982
  at: '2026-08-01T20:40:44Z'  # 1982
  by: agent  # 1982
  actor: jgstern_agent  # 1982
  clock: 1  # 1982
  nonce: '1982'  # 1982
  data:  # 1982
    kind: work_item  # 1982
    title: "compact's default select_by_coverage never applies is_excluded_kind while its two sibling entry points do; noise kinds leak into default output"  # 1982
    status: todo_hard  # 1982
    priority: 2  # 1982
    parent:  # 1982
    tags:  # 1982
    - linker_gap  # 1982
    isbefore: []  # 1982
    duplicate_of: []  # 1982
    not_duplicate_of: []  # 1982
    pr_ref:  # 1982
    description: "Found during the WI-zulij validation re-probe (2026-08-01, dev 529e4aebe3). Verified in source.\n\ncompact.py has three selection/format entry points and they DISAGREE about whether the canonical\nis_excluded_kind predicate applies:\n\n  compact.py:1421  select_by_tokens            -- applies it\n  compact.py:1720  format_tiered_behavior_map  -- applies it\n  compact.py:890-1357  select_by_coverage      -- DOES NOT. This is the DEFAULT compact path.\n\nVerified: grep for is_excluded_kind in compact.py returns exactly four hits -- the docstring at\n:40, the import at :87, and the two call sites at :1421 and :1720. There is no call inside\nselect_by_coverage's line range.\n\nMEASURED CONSEQUENCE (from the WI-zulij probe, independently reproduced by a second agent using\nthe imported predicate rather than a hand-rolled set): at --max-symbols 10 across the eight 07-17\nbakeoff maps, 17 of 80 emitted nodes are kinds the predicate rejects -- file 14, variable 2,\npackage 1. \"file\" is in EXCLUDED_KINDS in selection/filters.py. The two agents' K=100 numbers\ndisagree on the denominator because one run used an inconsistent --min-symbols, so treat the\nK=10 figure as the sound one and re-measure K=100 before citing it.\n\nWHY IT MATTERS BEYOND TIDINESS: the excluded kinds are excluded precisely because they have high\ncentrality without representing useful code, so leaking them into the default path's ranked\noutput puts noise at the top of what the tool advertises as its most important symbols. On the\n07-17 maps the leading emitted nodes include run*.sh and install.sh shell files and a\ncompletions script -- i.e. the noise is not evenly distributed, it concentrates at the head.\n\nRELATIONSHIP TO WI-batit: this is plausibly a partial root cause of the ordering/noise face\ntracked there, since the leading noise nodes measured are precisely EXCLUDED_KINDS members that\nthe default path never filters. Confirm rather than assume -- WI-batit's own framing is about\nseed ranking, and the seeds are force-included ahead of the ranked fill by a separate mechanism\n(compact.py:1247), so the two can both be contributing.\n\nOpen question the fix has to answer rather than assume: whether select_by_coverage's omission is\nan oversight or a deliberate choice for the coverage-driven path (coverage is computed over the\nfull graph, so filtering kinds mid-selection changes what coverage means). Read the coverage stop\nlogic before adding the call.\n\nNOT tagged awaits_bakeoff_validation: no quantitative bakeoff-improvement claim has been made\nyet. Tag at merge time if the fix ships with one."  # 1982
    fields: {}  # 1982
- op: discuss  # a6bc
  at: '2026-08-01T23:16:03Z'  # a6bc
  by: agent  # a6bc
  actor: jgstern_agent  # a6bc
  clock: 2  # a6bc
  nonce: a6bc  # a6bc
  message: "SCOPE NARROWED, NOT CLOSED, by the WI-zulij filter extraction (PR #155, dev 5e4fbcf7a4).\n\nThis item was filed as \"compact's three entry points disagree on whether is_excluded_kind\napplies\". That is still true, but the shape has changed and the earlier assumption that WI-zulij\nwould subsume it is WRONG -- recording the correction rather than leaving it implied.\n\nBEFORE: select_by_tokens (compact.py:1421) and format_tiered_behavior_map (:1720) applied the\nis_excluded_kind DENYLIST; the default select_by_coverage applied NOTHING.\n\nNOW: the default applies the KEY_SYMBOL_KINDS ALLOWLIST (via selection.filters.key_symbols), and\nthe two siblings still apply the denylist. So the default is no longer unfiltered -- the measured\n17-of-80 noise-kind leak at K=10 that this item was filed on is gone, because every kind in that\nleak (file, variable, package) is outside the allowlist.\n\nWHAT SURVIVES: the three entry points still do not share ONE predicate, and allowlist and denylist\nare not complements. They disagree on `variable` -- in KEY_SYMBOL_KINDS because Terraform/HCL\nvariables are a real declaration surface, in EXCLUDED_KINDS because CSS custom properties are\nzero-edge noise -- and on any kind that is in neither set, which the default now drops and the\nsiblings keep. A denylist-only variant was measured during the WI-zulij work and rejected on\nevidence (9.4/10 sketch agreement vs 10/10 for the allowlist, missing two repos outright), so\nconverging the three on is_excluded_kind is NOT the right unification direction; converging them\non the key-symbol policy is the candidate worth evaluating.\n\nSo the remaining question is narrower and now decidable: should select_by_tokens and\nformat_tiered_behavior_map ALSO move to key_symbols, giving compact one population across all\nthree of its surfaces? That is a behavior change to the token-budget and tiered views and needs\nits own measurement, not an assumption."  # a6bc
- op: discuss  # 747d
  at: '2026-10-01T01:07:28Z'  # 747d
  by: agent  # 747d
  actor: jgstern_agent  # 747d
  clock: 3  # 747d
  nonce: 747d  # 747d
  message: "PREMISE CHECK 2026-09-30 (dev 134a06d505): MISPREMISED (the leak is live, but not where the title puts it).\nThe 08-01 discussion entry predates fa7ae4e388 (WI-zulij, \"connected core by default\", 2026-08-02 01:25Z), which made connectivity the DEFAULT: cli.py:5332 `connectivity_aware = getattr(args, \"connectivity\", True)`, flags at cli.py:10915 / :9787. format_compact_behavior_map (compact.py:1203) applies production_edges + key_symbols ONLY under `if not connectivity_aware:` (compact.py:1259-1261), and the comment above it exempts connectivity mode on purpose (a file node can be the only bridge). select_by_connectivity (compact.py:711) applies no kind filter. So:\n  - select_by_coverage is NOT the default any more; it runs only under --no-connectivity, where the KEY_SYMBOL_KINDS allowlist applies.\n  - the DEFAULT path applies NEITHER the allowlist NOR is_excluded_kind, and seeds are not narrowed either.\n  - select_by_tokens (:1523) and format_tiered_behavior_map (:1822) still apply is_excluded_kind (the latter also drops is_external_boundary).\nBehavioural check (self-survey of this repo at 134a06d505, via the board): `hypergumbo compact --input self.json --max-symbols 10` (default) -> 4 of 10 nodes are kind `file` (pyproject.toml [project.scripts] lines 55-57 and 60; all 4 are in behavior_map.entrypoints, i.e. seeds) and 4 are `external_symbol` at <external> (hypergumbo_tracker.cli:main, :textconv_main, hypergumbo_core.cli:main, time:monotonic); the other 2 are functions. Same with --no-connectivity -> 0 excluded kinds, 0 non-key kinds.\nSo the 08-01 statement \"the measured 17-of-80 leak is gone\" was true for ~2 hours; on today's default it is back: the 4 file nodes enter as seeds, the 4 external_symbols (not entrypoints) as select_by_connectivity picks.\nProposed correction: retitle to name the connectivity default path (select_by_connectivity / its seed list) as the unfiltered surface, and add external_symbol boundary nodes to the leaked set. The open question becomes: narrow the connectivity SEEDS to key symbols (seeds are not bridges) and drop external boundary nodes as the tiered view does, while leaving real bridge picks unfiltered? Needs its own measurement against WI-zulij's connectivity numbers."  # 747d
- op: update  # 28ba
  at: '2026-10-01T01:36:15Z'  # 28ba
  by: agent  # 28ba
  actor: jgstern_agent  # 28ba
  clock: 4  # 28ba
  nonce: 28ba  # 28ba
  set:  # 28ba
    title: "compact's default connectivity path (select_by_connectivity, default since fa7ae4e388) applies no kind filter: file seeds and external boundary nodes lead the default output"  # 28ba
    description: "Found during the WI-zulij validation re-probe (2026-08-01, dev 529e4aebe3).\n\ncompact's DEFAULT path is connectivity mode (select_by_connectivity), the default since fa7ae4e388 (WI-zulij, \"connected core by default\"; cli.py:5332 `connectivity_aware = getattr(args, \"connectivity\", True)`). It applies NO kind filter: format_compact_behavior_map (compact.py:1203) applies production_edges + key_symbols only under `if not connectivity_aware:` (compact.py:1259-1261), and select_by_connectivity (compact.py:711) filters nothing. The exemption is deliberate (the comment above :1259: a file node can be the only bridge between two islands), but it also leaves the SEED list unfiltered.\n\ncompact's selection surfaces therefore apply three different populations:\n  select_by_connectivity (default)          -- no filter (no allowlist, no is_excluded_kind, boundary nodes kept)\n  select_by_coverage (--no-connectivity)    -- KEY_SYMBOL_KINDS allowlist via selection.filters.key_symbols\n  select_by_tokens (compact.py:1523) and\n  format_tiered_behavior_map (:1822)        -- is_excluded_kind denylist (tiered also drops is_external_boundary)\n\nMEASURED (self-analysis map of this repo, dev 134a06d505): `hypergumbo compact --input self.json --max-symbols 10` -> 4 of 10 emitted nodes are kind `file` (pyproject.toml [project.scripts] lines, all four in behavior_map.entrypoints, i.e. seeds) and 4 are `external_symbol` boundary nodes at <external>; 2 are functions. With --no-connectivity: 0 excluded kinds, 0 non-key kinds. The noise concentrates at the HEAD of what the tool advertises as its most important symbols. Why the console-script targets surface as external_symbol nodes at all is its own defect: WI-lipal-tikuf-pimob-disig-hojod-pimid-kisos-fihoj.\n\nAllowlist and denylist are not complements: they disagree on `variable` (in KEY_SYMBOL_KINDS for Terraform/HCL, in EXCLUDED_KINDS for CSS custom properties) and on any kind in neither set. A denylist-only variant was measured during WI-zulij and rejected (9.4/10 sketch agreement vs 10/10 for the allowlist), so converging on is_excluded_kind is not the right direction.\n\nOPEN QUESTION the fix must answer, with its own measurement against WI-zulij's connectivity numbers (isolated-node rate, containment): narrow the connectivity SEEDS to key symbols (seeds are not bridges) and drop external boundary nodes as the tiered view does, while leaving real bridge picks unfiltered? Separately: should select_by_tokens and format_tiered_behavior_map move to key_symbols so compact has one population?\n\nNOT tagged awaits_bakeoff_validation: no quantitative bakeoff-improvement claim has been made yet. Tag at merge time if the fix ships with one.\nRevised 2026-09-30 from the premise check (see discussion)."  # 28ba
